From f4f36213ee45d888598ad2a4cb62e952aaa53e34 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: reaper <theunbounddeveloper@outlook.com>
Date: Sat, 28 Nov 2026 12:47:08 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] Web server: add-on page sheet, placeholders for removed
 hooks, device pictures and types, ASUS Router app opt-in

- Add-on pages (REAPER-ADDON-SKIN): user<N>.asp, and an add-on's own copy of a page Reaper no longer ships, get the
  add-on sheet (reaper/reaper_addon.css), the shell bounce, the colour-blind block and the page token. They had
  shown the stock banner, menu and tabs since the stock skin left.
- Removed page hooks (REAPER-HOOK-PLACEHOLDER): nine hooks add-on pages still use as values (apps_info,
  bwdpi_appStat, bwdpi_wanStat, dns_appStat, dns_wanStat, dns_status, usb_is_exist, cpu_core_num, get_label_mac)
  print an empty value of the right kind and one log line per hook per boot instead of nothing.
- Guest portal look: get_customized_attribute takes a profile id of 1 to 13 digits only.
- Device pictures and types (REAPER-DEVICON): reaper_dev.cgi gains set_icon, del_icon, set_type, icon_list and
  icon_get (POST, page token, same origin; PNG / JPEG / WebP checked by content, 32 KB each, 256 pictures, refused
  when /jffs is nearly full; written with O_EXCL | O_NOFOLLOW and a rename). The old paths are closed: the picture
  field of the settings handler, get_usericon_md5.cgi, backup_all_usericon.cgi and upload_all_usericon.cgi.
  Clearing a device's name no longer drops its type.
- ASUS Router app (REAPER-APP-OPTIN): reaper_app_allow, off at factory. With it on, a request skips the cross-site
  refusal, the Referer checks, the page token and the POST-only rule only when its User-Agent is the app's, it
  arrived on the LAN-side listener and its sender is on the main network (IPv4 inside the LAN subnet, IPv6 on the LAN
  bridge). One decision per request (reaper_app_exempt); one log line on first use per boot, and one (at most every
  10 s) for a request that names the app from anywhere else. With it off nothing changes. The switch is in the full
  backup only and is watched by the Security Review.
- Wireless Log: the station list carries the Rx and Tx retry counters.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>
